WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.224 --> 00:00:21.005
Marius slowly climbed the steps to his apartment, his heart heavy with disappointment.

2
00:00:21.025 --> 00:00:25.906
"Monsieur Marius, you seem sad," said a voice behind him.

3
00:00:25.926 --> 00:00:27.167
"What's wrong?"

4
00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:31.908
At the top of the stairs, he turned around and found the older Jondrette girl.

5
00:00:32.564 --> 00:00:34.266
"Nothing's wrong," he said harshly.

6
00:00:34.286 --> 00:00:35.427
"Leave me alone."

7
00:00:35.447 --> 00:00:41.091
"No, you gave me something to eat; now let me help you," she pleaded.

8
00:00:41.111 --> 00:00:43.754
"I help my father all the time.

9
00:00:44.474 --> 00:00:49.419
Do you need me to deliver a message, or follow someone, or find out an address?"

10
00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.222
Marius realized that she might be useful after all.

11
00:00:53.242 --> 00:00:55.724
"You brought that old man and his daughter here.

12
00:00:56.304 --> 00:00:57.225
Do you know where they live?"

13
00:00:57.245 --> 00:01:05.066
"No, I met them at the church, but I can find out the address of the beautiful young

14
00:01:05.146 --> 00:01:06.527
lady if you wish."

15
00:01:07.588 --> 00:01:13.491
The bitterness with which she said "beautiful young lady" made Marius cringe, but he needed her assistance.

16
00:01:14.932 --> 00:01:16.512
"Yes, please do that for me."

17
00:01:17.113 --> 00:01:19.694
Marius entered his apartment and dropped into a chair.

18
00:01:20.675 --> 00:01:22.576
So much had happened since that morning.

19
00:01:23.236 --> 00:01:30.440
His angel had reappeared and then disappeared and now— "I tell you I'm sure I recognized him!"

20
00:01:31.476 --> 00:01:35.958
Monsieur Jondrette's angry voice from the room next door cut suddenly through Marius' thoughts.

21
00:01:36.878 --> 00:01:40.860
Marius climbed upon the table once more and peered through his spy hole.

22
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:46.762
Monsieur Jondrette had just come in and was taking off the coat that Monsieur Leblanc had given him.

23
00:01:46.782 --> 00:01:49.783
"Are you positive it's the same man?"

24
00:01:50.244 --> 00:01:51.504
asked Madame Jondrette.

25
00:01:52.124 --> 00:01:54.205
"Why didn't he recognize you?"

26
00:01:55.206 --> 00:01:56.986
Monsieur Jondrette stroked his beard.

27
00:01:57.006 --> 00:02:05.645
"Because I am in disguise, but even after all these years, I knew him immediately and the girl

28
00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.606
too. Don't you remember that girl who used to live with us?"

29
00:02:08.626 --> 00:02:11.167
"That girl!"

30
00:02:11.487 --> 00:02:15.768
Madame Jondrette's voice was a mixture of surprise, rage, and hatred.

31
00:02:15.788 --> 00:02:24.050
"Impossible! My daughters go barefoot and don't have a decent dress between them while her outfit must be

32
00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.791
worth at least two hundred francs!"

33
00:02:26.951 --> 00:02:29.772
"I'm telling you again that I recognized the two of them."

34
00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.601
Madame Jondrette shook her head in disbelief.

35
00:02:32.621 --> 00:02:36.223
"But Cosette used to be so ugly!

36
00:02:36.243 --> 00:02:42.665
You're saying she's that horrible, beautiful young lady who looked at my girls with such pity?

37
00:02:42.685 --> 00:02:46.607
Oh, I'd like to stomp her heart out!"

38
00:02:47.668 --> 00:02:49.248
"We'll do better than that, my dear.

39
00:02:49.909 --> 00:02:51.369
The old man will make us rich."

40
00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:53.850
Madame Jondrette looked puzzled.

41
00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:57.592
"It's all arranged," said her husband.

42
00:02:58.188 --> 00:03:00.569
"While I was out, I talked to some men and bought this."

43
00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.952
He showed her a chisel, and then laid the blade in the fire.

44
00:03:04.972 --> 00:03:10.055
"It may come in handy later if he won't cooperate."

45
00:03:11.035 --> 00:03:13.296
Marius could not believe what he was hearing.

46
00:03:13.817 --> 00:03:18.679
It appeared that Monsieur Leblanc—and perhaps Ursula too—was in grave danger.

47
00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.161
He slipped out of his apartment and went to the police station.

48
00:03:22.181 --> 00:03:27.304
"The chief of police isn't in," said an office boy when Marius arrived at the station.

49
00:03:28.368 --> 00:03:31.189
"But you can speak to an inspector if it's important."

50
00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:37.492
Marius nodded and the boy led him to an office, where a tall man was standing near the

51
00:03:37.532 --> 00:03:39.693
fire. "What do you want?"

52
00:03:40.193 --> 00:03:41.134
asked the inspector.

53
00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:44.135
"It's a very urgent matter," said Marius.

54
00:03:44.155 --> 00:03:46.836
"Then you'd better speak quickly."

55
00:03:47.476 --> 00:03:51.938
Marius told the inspector how he'd overheard the plot to ambush Monsieur Leblanc.

56
00:03:53.279 --> 00:03:58.034
He didn't know Leblanc's real name or address, but he was sure that the old man was in

57
00:03:58.094 --> 00:04:03.978
danger. This was all going to take place at six o'clock in the old Gorbeau house.

58
00:04:05.019 --> 00:04:06.700
The inspector raised his eyebrows.

59
00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.622
"The old Gorbeau house?"

60
00:04:08.642 --> 00:04:10.343
"Are you familiar with it?"

61
00:04:10.363 --> 00:04:12.144
"Indeed I am."

62
00:04:12.405 --> 00:04:15.207
The inspector reached into a drawer and pulled out a pistol.

63
00:04:16.107 --> 00:04:19.090
"Take this and go back to spying from your room.

64
00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.012
My men and I will be hiding in the neighborhood.

65
00:04:22.456 --> 00:04:26.899
When the situation is at its most dangerous, fire the pistol and we'll rush in."

66
00:04:27.979 --> 00:04:31.021
Marius took the gun and hid it in his waistcoat.

67
00:04:31.041 --> 00:04:37.545
"By the way," said the policeman, "if you need me before then, send a message to me here.

68
00:04:38.266 --> 00:04:40.827
My name is Inspector Javert."

69
00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:44.669
Marius went home and tiptoed into his apartment.

70
00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.632
There was only half an hour before Leblanc was due to return.

71
00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:54.718
As Marius climbed on top of his table, he could hear Monsieur Jondrette quizzing his daughters.

72
00:04:54.738 --> 00:04:59.199
"You saw the housekeeper go out, but what about the fellow next door?"

73
00:04:59.219 --> 00:05:03.100
"I heard him leave a while ago," said the older daughter.

74
00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:08.402
"He always goes out for his supper around this time and stays away for several hours."

75
00:05:08.422 --> 00:05:11.943
"You'd better check just to be sure."

76
00:05:13.023 --> 00:05:16.584
Marius dropped to his hands and knees and silently crawled under his bed.

77
00:05:17.128 --> 00:05:20.090
He'd just hidden himself when he saw his door open.

78
00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:23.532
"He's gone out, Papa," said the older girl.

79
00:05:23.552 --> 00:05:25.293
"His key is in the door."

80
00:05:25.313 --> 00:05:28.034
"Go in anyway," called her father.

81
00:05:28.955 --> 00:05:32.677
The girl entered the room with a candle and walked straight toward the bed.

82
00:05:33.157 --> 00:05:34.398
But she didn't look under it.

83
00:05:35.779 --> 00:05:40.462
Instead she headed for the mirror, where she gazed at herself and hummed a song.

84
00:05:41.502 --> 00:05:44.264
Meanwhile Marius was trembling under the bed.

85
00:05:44.788 --> 00:05:47.110
He couldn't believe that she didn't hear him breathing.

86
00:05:48.231 --> 00:05:49.772
"What are you doing over there?"

87
00:05:50.072 --> 00:05:51.853
called Monsieur Jondrette from next door.

88
00:05:51.873 --> 00:05:58.418
"I'm checking under all the furniture," said the daughter as she continued to arrange her hair in the

89
00:05:58.458 --> 00:06:00.759
mirror. "Come back here!

90
00:06:01.119 --> 00:06:02.600
It's time for you to go out."

91
00:06:03.361 --> 00:06:06.303
The girl left and Marius crawled from under the bed.

92
00:06:07.364 --> 00:06:12.647
He dusted himself off and climbed the table just in time to hear Jondrette giving instructions to his

93
00:06:12.687 --> 00:06:18.315
daughters. They were to stand guard at each end of the street and come back immediately at the

94
00:06:18.375 --> 00:06:20.036
first sign of anything strange.

95
00:06:20.977 --> 00:06:24.079
The girls left and Jondrette began to pace the room.

96
00:06:24.099 --> 00:06:26.361
"Do you know what we need?"

97
00:06:26.721 --> 00:06:27.682
he said to his wife.

98
00:06:27.702 --> 00:06:29.403
"Two more chairs."

99
00:06:29.423 --> 00:06:31.344
"No problem.

100
00:06:31.785 --> 00:06:33.226
I'll get them from the neighbor's."

101
00:06:34.206 --> 00:06:38.850
Before Marius could hide under the bed, Madame Jondrette had entered his apartment.

102
00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:41.712
Fortunately she had not brought a candle.

103
00:06:42.472 --> 00:06:48.297
Marius flattened himself against the wall while she went directly to his chairs, picked them up, and left

104
00:06:48.357 --> 00:06:48.817
the room.

105
00:06:49.898 --> 00:06:53.901
Marius did not dare to breathe until she was safely on the other side of the wall.

106
00:06:53.921 --> 00:06:58.905
"Good!" said Monsieur Jondrette as he arranged the chairs facing each other.

107
00:06:58.925 --> 00:07:03.529
"Now take this lantern downstairs and wait for our guest."

108
00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.272
Marius peered around the Jondrettes' darkened room.

109
00:07:08.193 --> 00:07:13.684
He noticed a pile of rope and some metal objects on the floor, but he didn't recognize them

110
00:07:13.704 --> 00:07:16.465
for what they were: burglar's tools.

111
00:07:18.246 --> 00:07:23.227
Jondrette pulled a long carving knife from a drawer in the table and ran his finger along the

112
00:07:23.347 --> 00:07:28.509
edge. Then he hid it away again and sat down in one of Marius' chairs.

113
00:07:29.469 --> 00:07:33.510
For his part, Marius took the pistol from his pocket and cocked it.

114
00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:36.451
The gun made a distinct click.

115
00:07:37.451 --> 00:07:39.752
Jondrette started and half rose from his chair.

116
00:07:39.772 --> 00:07:40.552
"Who's there?"

117
00:07:41.684 --> 00:07:43.104
Marius didn't dare to move.

118
00:07:43.665 --> 00:07:46.966
Jondrette listened for a moment and then began to laugh.

119
00:07:50.987 --> 00:07:52.347
"What a fool I am!

120
00:07:52.827 --> 00:07:54.368
It's just the wall creaking."

121
00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:57.588
Marius kept his pistol in his hand.

122
00:07:58.709 --> 00:08:04.430
A church clock struck six o'clock, and Marius heard the sound of a carriage arriving outside.
